# Normalise line endings in the repository.
#
# Without this, every text file differs between the repository (LF) and a
# Windows checkout (CRLF), so git reports the whole file as modified on every
# clone. That makes `git status` useless for spotting real work -- the diff for
# one changed line is indistinguishable from a whole-file rewrite. It happened
# here: 20 files showed as modified when the only real edits were two.
#
# * text=auto  -- let git detect text, and normalise on commit.
# * eol=lf     -- check out with LF everywhere, including on Windows. The pack
#                 ships .bat and .cmd launchers, which are marked eol=crlf
#                 below because a Windows batch file with LF endings misbehaves.
#
# Fixes the existing mess in one commit; after this the tree settles.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Launchers run under cmd.exe, which wants CRLF.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Binary. Never touch.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.pk3 binary
*.wad binary
*.ipk3 binary
*.sf2 binary
*.dll binary
*.exe binary
*.pk7 binary
*.deh binary
*.map binary
*.lmp binary